            "links": []
        },
        {
            "step_number": 2,
            "title": "Detach L-Board Cable and Remove L-Board",
            "images": [
                {
                    "url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/LCYDYdGDyTgUk1TS.medium",
                    "thumbnail_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/LCYDYdGDyTgUk1TS.200x150"
                },
                {
                    "url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/XjrsVNeP12qsarrR.medium",
                    "thumbnail_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/XjrsVNeP12qsarrR.200x150"
                },
                {
                    "url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/IwKCMM4LwNnK1LIq.medium",
                    "thumbnail_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/IwKCMM4LwNnK1LIq.200x150"
                }
            ],
            "instructions": [
                "Place fingers above and beyond Bear Quilting Patch and pull l-board gently toward you.",
                "Rotate left side of l-board toward you and to the right to access cable.",
                "Gently remove yellow cable."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/168487/357145",
            "add_comment_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Bernina+350+PE+L-Board+D5+Capacitor+Replacement/<#>",
            "links": []
        },
        {
            "step_number": 3,
            "title": "Remove L-Board's Cover",
            "images": [],
            "instructions": [
                "Remove 4 screws with Torx T-10 driver.",
                "Foreground is the base, pull it toward you and cover (background/closest to table) stays behind.",
                "Base, with l-board attached, is shown in last picture."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/168487/357146",
            "add_comment_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Bernina+350+PE+L-Board+D5+Capacitor+Replacement/<#>",
            "links": []
        },
        {
            "step_number": 4,
            "title": "Examine L-Board Capacitors",
            "images": [],
            "instructions": [
                "Capacitor attached to D5 is bulging out the top and is pushing its innards out the bottom.",
                "If damaged like the one in photograph, obtain a replacement capacitor for D5 that is rated for long-life, 25 volts, and 100 µF, I found one at MicroCenter for $0.99."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/168487/357149",
            "add_comment_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Bernina+350+PE+L-Board+D5+Capacitor+Replacement/<#>",
            "links": []
        },
        {
            "step_number": 5,
            "title": "Remove D5 Capacitor",
            "images": [],
            "instructions": [
                "I used a soldering gun to wick and to remove as much solder from back side of board where D5 is marked.",
                "After solder is removed, I gently bent the capacitors pins so they were straightened and ready to remove from hole.",
                "Add flux to the board, heat the capacitor's pins, and use a [tweezers](https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Bernina+350+PE+L-Board+D5+Capacitor+Replacement/<https:/www.ifixit.com/products/tweezers>) to pull on the D5 capacitor."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/168487/357150",
            "add_comment_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Bernina+350+PE+L-Board+D5+Capacitor+Replacement/<#>",
            "links": [
                {
                    "name": "Tweezers",
                    "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/products/tweezers",
                    "image": "https://cart-products.cdn.ifixit.com/cart-products/eQGTt3iN1MmOAQDy.thumbnail"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "step_number": 6,
            "title": "Install Replacement Capacitor",
            "images": [],
            "instructions": [
                "Slide the replacement capacitor into the D5 board holes.",
                "Heat the board and apply solder.",
                "Replacement capacitor looks like pictures to the left."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/168487/357151",
            "add_comment_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Bernina+350+PE+L-Board+D5+Capacitor+Replacement/<#>",
            "links": []
        },
        {
            "step_number": 7,
            "title": "",
            "images": [],
            "instructions": [
                "Replace cover on l-board and reinsert 4 screws.",
                "Gently place extra slack from yellow l-board cable back inside sewing machine body.",
                "In reverse, return to Step 2, complete, and conclude with Step 1 to continue reassembling sewing machine and test."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/168487/357152",
            "add_comment_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Bernina+350+PE+L-Board+D5+Capacitor+Replacement/<#>",
            "links": []
